# Dev Caddyfile — admin endpoint + local CA, plus ONE placeholder site so an HTTP server
# (srv0) exists for Loskai to discover and push routes into. Without any site there is no
# apps.http.servers, so Loskai has no server to append routes to.
#
# The hostname below is an arbitrary placeholder. In dev, `local_certs` makes Caddy issue
# an internal cert per routed name on demand, so this does NOT need to match Loskai's
# BASE_DOMAIN — set that wherever you like (Loskai's UI or the backend env); Caddy doesn't
# need it here.
#
# DO NOT set BASE_DOMAIN=localhost to "line them up". A site block with no handlers adapts
# to a `"terminal": true` route with nothing to handle the request, and the adapter puts it
# first — so every route Loskai pushes for a name it matches is shadowed and Caddy answers
# an empty 200 instead of proxying. Keeping this placeholder *different* from BASE_DOMAIN is
# what makes the dev rig work, and it is the reason that defect survived to 2026-09-05 in
# the co-located Caddyfile, where BASE_DOMAIN really is substituted here. See
# docs/guides/troubleshooting.md#a-blank-page-or-an-empty-200.
#
# (Production differs: the real wildcard `*.BASE_DOMAIN` cert is obtained via DNS challenge,
# so there Caddy DOES need BASE_DOMAIN in its own env — see the root Caddyfile + PLAN.md.)

{
	admin 0.0.0.0:2019
	local_certs
}

*.localhost {
	tls internal
}

# Certificate onboarding (Phase 10a) — served over plain HTTP on :80 so it's reachable
# by IP *before* Caddy's internal CA is trusted (installing that CA is the page's whole
# job — it can't sit behind the untrusted cert). This is a SEPARATE Caddy server from the
# :443 routing one; Loskai discovers the routing server by its :443 listener, so it never
# pushes routes here. In dev, reach it at http://localhost:8081/ (compose maps 8081:80).
:80 {
	# The internal root CA, streamed live from Caddy's PKI (unique per install — never
	# committed). Appears once Caddy has initialised its `local` CA.
	handle /caddy-root.crt {
		root * /data/caddy/pki/authorities/local
		rewrite * /root.crt
		header Content-Type application/x-x509-ca-cert
		file_server
	}
	# Everything else → the onboarding page (index.html).
	handle {
		root * /srv/setup
		file_server
	}
}
